A('## 6. How to read the "planning expectation"')
A('')
A('The backtests are optimistic in ways that cannot all be measured, so each build idea carries an explicit haircut. **This is judgment, not a statistical estimate.**')
A('')
A('* **Sharpe:** 50%–80% of the idea\'s **2015+** Sharpe (the more recent and less-flattering period; the same idea earned much more in 2004–2014).')
A('* **CAGR:** 6% (cash) + Sharpe × 2015+ volatility − volatility²/2.')
A('* **Max drawdown:** the full-sample worst drawdown × 1.25–1.5 (the sample contains 2008 and 2020 but not every possible path).')
A('* **Portfolio improvement:** 50%–80% of the measured 2015+ improvement.')
A('* **Why the haircut:** (i) survivorship — only ~2% of symbols are delisted (removing the known delisted names changed results by <0.02 Sharpe, so the bias comes from names missing entirely and cannot be measured here); (ii) the factor pairs were chosen after seeing single-factor results; '
  '(iii) 2015+ decay — price-based IC was 30–40% lower after 2014; (iv) the proxy ignores execution frictions (circuit limits, partial fills).')
A('')
